 ## Overview
-Octree Traversal with Min/Max Pruning is an acceleration technique for ray tracing isosurfaces in scalar volumes stored in an octree. It solves the problem of efficiently skipping transparent or empty regions during rendering by using hierarchical min/max scalar value bounds to prune nodes that cannot contain the target isovalue [S2][S3]. Unlike sibling methods that may rely on brick-level classifications or view-dependent working sets, this method embeds the acceleration structure directly within the volume data container, allowing for interactive transfer function changes by recomputing classification based on stored scalar ranges [S1][S4, unofficial]. It builds on [Empty Space Skipping with Octree](1610-empty-space-skipping-with-octree.md).
